---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Josh Rutz · game maker & team builder" description="I make games that move people. I build teams that own their work.">
  <header class="hero"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow reveal">Game maker · Team builder</div>
    <h1 class="reveal">I make <span class="live">games</span> that move people.</h1>
    <p class="lede reveal">That standard has guided every choice I've made. I'm a game
      director aiming to build a <span class="live">studio</span>, because leading is
      how great people make great games.</p>
    <div class="cta reveal">
      <a class="btn" href="/projects">See the work</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/resume">Read the résumé</a>
    </div>
  </div></header>

  <section><div class="wrap">
    <div class="label reveal" id="why-line">Why games<span class="rule"></span></div>
    <p class="body reveal">I've loved games my whole life, both playing and making them. They've helped
      me grow as a person and given me purpose. I hope to make games to help inspire others to find
      purpose as well.</p>

    <div class="label reveal">The work<span class="rule"></span></div>
    <a class="panel reveal" href="/projects">
      <div class="kind">Platform</div><h3>Zipix</h3>
      <p>A mobile-first micro-game platform. Every game is one complete experience in about a minute. You pick it up, you finish something, you put it down.</p>
    </a>

    <div class="label reveal">Where this goes<span class="rule"></span></div>
    <p class="big reveal">The studio I'm aiming to build will be an elite, autonomous cell.</p>
    <p class="body reveal">A small group that operates at a high level on its own, which makes it valuable
      inside a bigger organization or standing alone. Leading a great team is how great games get
      made, and that's why I want to build one.</p>
    <p class="body reveal">People do their best work when the company's goals and their own line up. My job
      as a leader is to find those two directions and align them as tightly as possible. I hand people
      real responsibility early, more than they think they can hold, then I clear the path so they can
      carry it. The leader grants the autonomy. The work supplies the purpose. The worker loves
      mastering their craft.</p>

    <div class="label reveal">Find me<span class="rule"></span></div>
    <p class="body reveal" style="margin-bottom:22px">I'm always glad to talk with people building
      ambitious things in games. And I'll talk about playing them, and the theory underneath, for as
      long as you'll let me.</p>
    <a class="btn accent reveal" href="mailto:joshrutz989@gmail.com">Reach out</a>
  </div></section>
</Base>

<script>
  // the stick figure hops between the section's separator lines as you scroll — jumping up or
  // falling down to whichever divider is nearest the middle (single source: /lib/stickman.js)
  import '../../lib/stickman.js';
  const host = document.getElementById('why-line')?.closest('.wrap');
  const S = window.Stickman;
  if (host && S) {
    const lines = Array.from(host.querySelectorAll('.label .rule'));
    const runner = S.createRunner({ mount: host, color: 'var(--ink)', dustColor: 'var(--ink-faint)' });
    S.attachScrollHop(runner, { host, lines });
  }
</script>
